01| [No Name]  3 [Scratch]                                                                                                                                        X
02| <CR> open  │  D digest  │  s sort  │  ]b breaking  │  ? keys          │Move to a commit to see its message here
03|plugins updated · ################ · overview · 3 changed, 6 commits, 1│~
04|                                                                       │~
05|! breaking  telescope.nvim  3237450..19281ca  3 commits                │~
06|╭─────────────────────────────────────────────plugins report─────────────────────────────────────────────╮
07|│ <CR>  On a plugin: its detail. On a commit in the digest: its plugin's detail, cursor on the commit    │
08|│ D  Breaking digest: the breaking commits of every plugin in one list                                   │
09|│ s  Cycle the sort: breaking first, name, number of commits, time of the update                         │
10|│ A  List the unchanged plugins too, or count them again                                                 │
11|│ ]b  Next / previous breaking commit not marked as seen                                                 │
12|│ m  Mark the commit under the cursor as seen, or every new commit of the plugin under it; again: unmark │
13|│ M  Mark every commit this view lists as seen                                                           │
14|│ o  Open in the browser: the commit, or on a plugin the compare page of its update; counts as seen      │
15|│ go  Open the compare page of the plugin's update, also from a commit line                              │
16|│ gy  Copy the URL `o` would open                                                                        │
17|│ y  Copy the short / full hash (on a plugin: the commit its update ended on)                            │
18|│ L  lazygit in the plugin's clone (lazygit can change the clone; the report itself never does)          │
19|│ S  The clone's git status and last five commits, read only                                             │
20|│ C  The plugin's CHANGELOG, in the tab the report was opened from                                       │
21|│ Q  The breaking commits into the quickfix list, opened in the tab the report was opened from           │
22|│ F  Jump to a plugin or a commit by name (picker)                                                       │
23|│ r  Read the clone under the cursor again (a failed one, say); for this tab only, nothing is stored     │
24|│ R  Build a new report (same mode), store it and show it                                                │
25|│ p  Show or hide the preview (follows the cursor)                                                       │
26|│ q  Close the report tab; the report stays, `:Git plugins` opens it again                               │
27|│ ?  List every one of these keys                                                                        │
